"answer": "According to the \"Eye Movement Disorders\" summary, strabismus is a disorder where the two eyes do not line up in the same direction, resulting in \"crossed eyes\" or \"walleye.\" Nystagmus involves fast, uncontrollable eye movements, sometimes called \"dancing eyes.\" The provided text does not state the exact percentage of patients with nystagmus who improve after eye muscle surgery; it only notes that there is no cure for most kinds of nystagmus."
